Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:17:21 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 077/230] Persist URL-recovered Telegram initData so reloads
 stay authenticated
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The URL fallback parsed tgWebAppData correctly on the first launch, but
applyTelegramUrlNormalization then rewrote the URL to strip Telegram's
fragment; Telegram appends that fragment only on the initial navigation, so
the next load (Telegram webviews reload often) arrived with nothing. With the
SDK script blocked in Iran the fragment was the only copy of the init data,
so a reload hit [auth:guest] initData=no and downgraded the user to a guest.
Keep the capture in sessionStorage (tab-scoped, like the ephemeral token) and
recover it whenever a load carries no fragment. Drop the temporary on-screen
Telegram debug dump now that the fallback is understood, and cover the reload
path with a unit test.

